9638,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017917460154657425,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":70.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.0035100002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"The Macerich Company is a fully integrated, self-managed, self-administered real estate investment trust (REIT). As a leading owner, operator, and developer of high-quality retail real estate in densely populated and attractive U.S. markets, Macerich's portfolio is concentrated in California, the Pacific Northwest, Phoenix/Scottsdale, and the Metro New York to Washington, D.C. corridor. Developing and managing properties that serve as community cornerstones, Macerich currently owns approximately 39 million square feet of real estate, consisting primarily of interests in 37 retail centers. The Macerich Company was incorporated in 1964 in Maryland and is based in Santa Monica, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jackson  Hsieh | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 596 people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Macerich Company (The) is a mid-cap real estate business with a $7.4B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 13.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 189% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 40% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3974613003095977},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(MAC) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/MAC_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_111226101801_1794496681.html","date":"2026-11-12","ti